---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspeacg18.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope – What Qualifies as an Investment Company" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Qualifying Criteria" },
        { id: "s4", label: "THE CORE PRINCIPLE – Fair Value Throughout, Regardless of Influence or Control" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Why This Override Exists" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example – Measuring a Controlled Investee at Fair Value" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IFRS 10's Investment Entity Exception" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">





<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Fair value information, not consolidated line items, is what investors in an investment company actually want</div><div class="principle">AcG-18 addresses HOW a QUALIFYING investment COMPANY accounts FOR its INVESTMENTS – REGARDLESS of the DEGREE of INFLUENCE or CONTROL held OVER a PARTICULAR investee, ALL investments ARE measured AT fair VALUE through NET income. THIS Guideline OVERRIDES the NORMAL ownership-BASED accounting FRAMEWORK (Sections 1591 and 3051 – see the COMPANION posters) an INVESTMENT company WOULD otherwise HAVE to APPLY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – What Qualifies as an Investment Company</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">An entity whose business purpose is investing for returns, not operational integration</div><div class="principle">An INVESTMENT company is AN entity WHOSE business PURPOSE is INVESTING funds FOR returns IN the FORM of INTEREST, dividends, OR capital APPRECIATION – WITH no PLAN to HOLD its INVESTMENTS indefinitely FOR strategic OR operational purposes.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Qualifying Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Investment purpose, portfolio management, and fair-value-based evaluation</div><div class="check-list"><span>Business purpose is investing funds for capital appreciation, investment income, or both</span><span>No plans for investees to become operationally integrated with the investment company</span><span>Ownership interests may be represented by units entitling the holder to a share of net assets</span><span>Investees are managed and evaluated collectively as a portfolio, on a fair value basis</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE CORE PRINCIPLE – Fair Value Throughout, Regardless of Influence or Control</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">No consolidation, no equity method – even for controlled investees</div><div class="text-supporting">A QUALIFYING investment COMPANY measures ALL of its INVESTMENTS at FAIR value, WITH changes RECOGNIZED directly IN net INCOME – THIS applies EVEN to INVESTMENTS where the INVESTMENT company HOLDS control (WHICH would OTHERWISE trigger CONSOLIDATION under Section 1591) or SIGNIFICANT influence (WHICH would OTHERWISE trigger the EQUITY method under SECTION 3051). NEITHER consolidation NOR the EQUITY method IS applied by a QUALIFYING investment COMPANY – FAIR value THROUGH net INCOME is the SOLE measurement BASIS, REGARDLESS of OWNERSHIP percentage OR degree OF influence.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Why This Override Exists</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fair value is simply more decision-useful for this specific business model</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR an ENTITY whose ENTIRE business MODEL is BUYING and SELLING investments FOR a RETURN, CONSOLIDATING a CONTROLLED investee'S individual ASSETS and LIABILITIES line-BY-line would OBSCURE, RATHER than illuminate, the INFORMATION genuinely RELEVANT to the INVESTMENT company'S own INVESTORS – WHO care ABOUT the AGGREGATE fair VALUE of the PORTFOLIO, NOT the OPERATIONAL details OF each UNDERLYING investee. FAIR value THROUGHOUT is SIMPLY the MORE decision-USEFUL measurement BASIS for THIS particular BUSINESS model.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example – Measuring a Controlled Investee at Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">No consolidation, despite a controlling stake</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A private equity fund holding a controlling stake</div><div class="wk-body">A qualifying investment company holds a 70% controlling interest in a portfolio company, originally invested at $4,000,000, now with an estimated fair value of $6,500,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">DESPITE holding a CONTROLLING interest, the INVESTMENT company does <strong>NOT</strong> consolidate the PORTFOLIO company – it SIMPLY measures the INVESTMENT at its $6,500,000 FAIR value, RECOGNIZING a $6,500,000 − $4,000,000 = <strong>$2,500,000</strong> gain DIRECTLY within NET income.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What AcG-18 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Basis for concluding the enterprise qualifies as an investment company</span><span>Fair value measurement techniques used for significant investments</span><span>Nature of significant investments, including any controlling or significant-influence relationships not consolidated or equity-accounted for</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether the enterprise genuinely qualifies as an investment company under all the required criteria</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of unquoted portfolio investments</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 10's Investment Entity Exception</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison – ASPE AcG-18 vs IFRS 10's investment entity exception</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE AcG-18</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 10 (2012 amendment)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Exemption from consolidating controlled investees</span><span>YES, for qualifying investment companies</span><span>YES, for qualifying investment entities – conceptually parallel</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">CONCEPTUALLY closely PARALLEL to IFRS 10'S OWN investment ENTITY exception, INTRODUCED internationally IN 2012 – BOTH frameworks INDEPENDENTLY concluded THAT fair value IS more decision-USEFUL than CONSOLIDATION for THIS specific BUSINESS model.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every investment company measurement lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fair value change on any investee</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized in net income, regardless of control or influence held</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1591</span><span>Subsidiaries – the general consolidation framework this Guideline overrides for a qualifying investment company</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3051</span><span>Investments – the general equity/cost method framework this Guideline overrides</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Investment company</div><div class="glossary-def">An entity whose business purpose is investing funds for capital appreciation or investment income, without plans for its investees to become operationally integrated.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Fair value throughout</div><div class="glossary-def">The measurement of all of an investment company's investments at fair value through net income, regardless of the degree of control or influence held.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspeacg18 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
